research/audit/wave14-coverage.json:170:  "attestation": "Alpha recovered the complete durable Wave14 record and audited all 25 scoped items, both page files, all 23 proof-bearing items and strict contracts, all 178 exact-final relationships, all 16 frozen Wave14-to-Wave11/Wave12/Wave13 barrier edges, all 66 distinct outside targets, all 59 proof-bearing top-100 spine items, and every required impact consumer without sampling. A7 covered exactly the ten recorded A4/A6 repair targets with paired DeepSeek/Terra verdicts; all nine initial rejection tuples have exact Alpha outcomes. A8 changed exactly two confirmed-fatal items, independently Terra-certified both repairs, dispositioned the sole consumer still-licensed, and rejudged exactly those two items. The repaired e theorem is DeepSeek keep/Terra reject; Alpha appended an exact-current false-positive adjudication because the cited ordered embeddings and canonical-natural positivity prove integer discreteness, so honesty leaves it without a judge-pass stamp. At A9, rendercheck found one hard source-line break inside the example's otherwise unchanged display. The orchestrator removed only that break, removed stale stamps, obtained exact-current Terra certification, dispositioned its empty consumer set, and rejudged only that repaired item; DeepSeek and Terra both kept it and the targeted stamp was refreshed. All ten required target pairs are covered and every current rejection has an exact nonfatal or false-positive disposition."
