research/frontier-13-dispatch/beta-smoke-batch-2.result.json:16:  "tail": "Added one honest runnable test to [Batch 2’s contract](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/frontier-13-batch-2.proof-contracts.json:437):\n\n- `lem-order-of-a-power-in-a-finite-cyclic-group`\n- Checks 1,098 cyclic-subgroup instances through order 200.\n\nValidation passes:\n\n```text\nfinite-smoke: 0 error(s), 1 check(s)\nproof-contract: 0 error(s), 0 warning(s), 67/67 item(s) checked\n```\n\nBlocker: full requested coverage is impossible within this dispatch’s write scope. The runner has no checks for the eight required `fs-`/`cex-` witnesses:\n\n- `fs-every-short-exact-sequence-of-groups-splits`\n- `fs-kernel-and-quotient-determine-a-group-extension`\n- `fs-an-abelian-group-has-an-abelian-automorphism-group`\n- `cex-unit-group-modulo-fifteen-is-not-cyclic`\n- `cex-euler-totient-need-not-be-the-unit-group-exponent`\n- `cex-cyclic-prime-square-extension-does-not-split`\n- `cex-a-complement-in-a-semidirect-product-need-not-be-normal`\n- `cex-a-subgroup-of-an-abelian-group-need-not-be-characteristic`\n\nThe other 58 contracts remain uncovered because none of the six registered checks applies; they need new congruence, unit-group, extension, semidirect-product, or automorphism enumerators, or have no appropriate finite family. I did not attach unrelated checks.\n\nI independently reran the binomial-congruence search: exactly 18,895 solvable instances, zero counterexamples. It cannot yet be made durable without adding a runner check. No unexpected counterexample to a true claim was found."
