research/frontier-13-dispatch/alpha-alpha-c.result.json:16:  "tail": "\n## Verdicts\n\n| pair | items | verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `erdos-hajnal-property-and-homogeneous-sets` (395) | 11 A / 8 B | **insufficient** |\n| `regular-pairs-and-induced-counting` (399) | 25 A / 8 B | **sufficient** |\n| `adjunctions-units-and-counits` (365.001) | 51 A / 9 B | **sufficient** |\n\n## The one insufficient pair\n\n**Order 395 never proves that any forbidden graph has the Erdős–Hajnal property.** It defines the property, refutes it for the class of all graphs, proves three invariances, states the conjecture — and stops. `ex-complete-and-empty-hereditary-classes-have-constant-one` is not this: \"complete graphs have EH constant 1\" says a complete graph is a clique; the real statement is \"$K_t$-**free** graphs are EH\", which is Ramsey's theorem and is absent.\n\nBeta's Chudnovsky locator stops at p. 2. Page 3 opens with exactly the missing material. Three additions, all provable from published items already in closure — no `requires` change, no split (11 → 14 items):\n\n- **$K_t$-free ⇒ EH**, from `thm-finite-graph-ramsey-binomial-bound` (I read it: $\\binom{s+t-2}{s-1}\\to(s,t)^2$, off-diagonal, exactly what's needed).\n- **$P_3$-free ⇒ $\\hom(G)\\ge\\sqrt n$** — every component is a clique, so $n\\le\\alpha\\omega\\le\\hom^2$; `graphs-walks-and-connectivity` already supplies 14 of this page's deps.\n- **Every graph on ≤ 3 vertices is EH**, from those two plus the scaffolded complement invariance.\n\n## Riehl locators — the alarm was a false positive\n\nDownloaded the PDF (build `D:20260728`) and read Chapter 4. §4.6 in the 2nd edition **is** \"Adjunctions, limits, and colimits\"; the adjoint functor theorems are Theorems 4.7.3/4.7.10/4.7.17 in §4.7, which Beta cites only for Lemma 4.7.1. Every page boundary in the locator is exact. The 12 numbers that look missing from the harvest are **displayed-equation numbers**, not environments. No first-edition locator was carried over.\n\nAlso verified against the text: MA-1 item 40 dropped to the Hom side and recorded; `def-floor-and-ceiling` genuinely does not exist in `library/`, and the drop is recorded twice; both B-leaf traps avoided by local construction; the RAPL split intact; the choice wording survived in four places, not three.\n\n## Three corrections on batch 6 (edits, not additions — headroom untouched)\n\n1. `cor-a-galois-connection-satisfies-fgf-equals-f-and-gfg-equals-g` asserts *equality* while depending only on a **preorder** definition. Riehl Cor. 4.2.10 says \"If $A$ and $B$ are **posets**…\" — without antisymmetry you get only $FGF\\cong F$. Title claims more than the proof gives.\n2. The ideal/variety example is *antitone* and cites the monotone `def-galois-connection`; Riehl homes it under Def. 4.4.1. Fixing it also gives `def-mutually-left-and-mutually-right-adjoint-contravariant-functors` its only consumer.\n3. `ex-the-maximal-subgroupoid-and-fractions-adjoint-triple` claims a triple but has no dependency supporting the groupoid-of-fractions left adjoint, and there is no localisation page anywhere in `plan-spec.json`. Recommend narrowing to the right adjoint.\n\n## Independently re-derived\n\n318 dependency edges across all six pages: **0 unresolved, 0 out-of-closure, 0 unpublished, 0 B-leaf**. Batch 4's pairs don't cite each other; batch 6 doesn't cite batch 5.\n\nTwo things worth the orchestrator's attention beyond the Beta routing: **batch 4's notes propose two-paragraph summaries for both B pages** — published B pages have zero bytes of body — and **the D1 edge `conjugacy-and-simplicity-in-the-symmetric-groups` is used by no item**; `def-abelianisation-of-a-group` is homed on `free-groups-and-presentations`, already reachable, so the step-0 rationale for that one edge is wrong. I didn't touch `plan-spec.json`.\n\nBatch 4's induced-removal chain closes as advertised, and the tower-bound titles are honest — Zhao's Thm 2.1.17 says verbatim \"We do not include the proof here\", so the decline is real. One wording fix required on `rem-tower-and-wowzer-bounds-in-regularity` (\"gives tower bounds\" must say *upper*), and one coverage gap: Zhao Exercises 2.1.22–2.1.25 sit inside §2.1 but outside the stated locator, and 2.1.24 is the half graph the notes cite.\n\nStanding by to re-check the routed fixes before step 4 splices. Steps 4, 6c and 8 belong to group A."
