research/defect-ledger.jsonl:455:{"defect_id":"frontier-12-D001","run":"frontier-12","at":"2026-08-13","class":"silent-runtime","subclass":"stage-unowned","severity":"fatal","location":"engine-stage","subject":"5-author","caught_at_stage":"5-author","caught_by_role":"orchestrator","disposition":"fixed","repair_cost":"none","prevention":{"kind":"mechanical","ref":"tools/run-supervisor.mjs holds the stage table and fires the next dispatch; built at the end of frontier-13 and never exercised until frontier-14"},"subclass_note":"Step 5 cleared at 06:28 with all twelve gates green. Instead of dispatching step 6 the orchestrator wrote a message describing what step 6 WOULD involve and ended the turn; the run sat idle until 10:41 - 4 hours 14 minutes - until the owner asked why it had stopped. Second session in a row. A cleared stage is a dispatch trigger, not a reporting checkpoint; the failure is invisible from the inside because the turn looks like good work.","evidence":[{"path":"/Users/ianx/.claude/projects/-Users-ianx-Projects-prestige-math-library/memory/autonomous-run-no-stage-pauses.md","anchor":"Measured cost, run frontier-12"},{"path":"research/frontier-14-PREVENTIONS.md","anchor":"B1. Pausing at a stage boundary"}],"source":"reconstructed"}
research/defect-ledger.jsonl:481:{"defect_id":"frontier-14-D429","run":"frontier-14","at":"2026-08-16","class":"silent-runtime","subclass":"prompt-transcription","severity":"nonfatal","location":"brief","subject":"research/frontier-14-brief-alpha-6c.md","caught_at_stage":"6c-cross","caught_by_role":"lead-alpha","disposition":"open","repair_cost":"none","prevention":{"kind":"process","ref":"generate a brief from the artifact it refers to, or point at that artifact and let the agent read it"},"subclass_note":"Step-10 machinery finding 13. The 6c brief Run facts table describes a DIFFERENT RUN entirely - symmetric polynomials, tensor products, Erdos-Hajnal, and frontier-13 named challenges - and its \"Named challenges\" section is written against them. The group Alphas own dispatches were correct so nothing downstream was misled, but a future session reading that brief for context would be. The step-0 record is the authority.","evidence":[{"path":"research/frontier-14-step10-report.md","anchor":"Findings about the machinery 13"}],"source":"reconstructed"}
research/defect-ledger.jsonl:484:{"defect_id":"frontier-14-D431","run":"frontier-14","at":"2026-08-16","class":"richness","subclass":"scope-loss","severity":"fatal","location":"engine-stage","subject":"stone-weierstrass-general","caught_at_stage":"4-splice","caught_by_role":"orchestrator","disposition":"fixed","repair_cost":"run-restart","prevention":{"kind":"mechanical","ref":"tools/manifest-integrity.mjs compares every manifest against a step-0 scope ledger and runs at every stage that gates the plan - a gate that reads current state cannot detect absence"},"subclass_note":"CLASS DEVIATION: recorded as richness/scope-loss rather than a runtime subclass, because the loss is content. A fully scaffolded A/B pair - 19 items, three verified sources, complete contracts, reviewed by an Alpha - was removed from the manifest, the coverage harvest and the contracts between steps 3 and 4. coverage-checklist, content-policy, validate-plan, precheck and the repo-wide sweep all stayed green: they validate what is IN the artifacts and none can see a page that is no longer there. The run reported 6/6 batches complete and would have shipped eight pairs where nine were planned. Found by counting authored pages against the plan. Cause: removing the orchestrator left no role able to add a requires edge, an Alpha marked the pair not-ready pending exactly that decision, and the splice resolved the deadlock by dropping it.","evidence":[{"path":"/Users/ianx/.claude/projects/-Users-ianx-Projects-prestige-math-library/memory/scope-loss-is-invisible-to-gates.md","anchor":"On frontier-14"},{"path":"research/frontier-14-step10-report.md","anchor":"What was built - batch 7"}],"source":"reconstructed"}
research/defect-ledger.jsonl:509:{"defect_id":"frontier-13-D052","run":"frontier-13","at":"2026-08-14","class":"silent-runtime","subclass":"other","severity":"fatal","location":"engine-stage","subject":"research/plan-spec.json requires","caught_at_stage":"unknown","caught_by_role":"orchestrator","disposition":"fixed","repair_cost":"rescope","prevention":{"kind":"process","ref":"at step 0 diff every pair design prerequisites against the transitive closure of the spec requires"},"subclass_note":"A pair prose design block and its plan-spec.json requires drift silently. adjunctions-units-and-counits - the largest fan-out in the plan, 197 unbuilt A pages downstream - is designed with SEVEN page prerequisites and the spec declared ONE. Three of the missing six were not reachable transitively at all, all published, all free to add. Nothing catches this until validate-plan raises undeclared-prereq at step 4, after the Beta has scaffolded and harvested; three landmark worked adjunctions would have had to be dropped or the pair re-scaffolded. The closed stage list has no step-0 id, so caught_at_stage is unknown; the prevention belongs at step 0, before scaffolding.","evidence":[{"path":"/Users/ianx/.claude/projects/-Users-ianx-Projects-prestige-math-library/memory/design-spec-requires-drift.md","anchor":"Measured on run frontier-13"}],"source":"reconstructed","should_have_caught":"1-scaffold"}
research/defect-ledger.jsonl:700:{"defect_id":"f16-c-r7-3","run":"frontier-16","at":"2026-08-20","class":"accuracy","subclass":"citation-truncated","severity":"fatal","location":"facts-block","subject":"thm-weierstrass-convergence-holomorphic-functions","batch":"7","caught_at_stage":"6a-read","caught_by_role":"reader","introduced_at_stage":"5-author","introduced_by_role":"beta","should_have_caught":"5-author","disposition":"fixed","repair_cost":"inline-fix","subclass_note":"R7-3 — thm-weierstrass-convergence-holomorphic-functions - **Location:** [L5] and contract citations [L5] and [L8]. - **Defect:** [L5] omitted the hypotheses that the difference function be holomorphic on a larger disc and that $0\\le r<R<S$. Separately, the contract quote for [L8] was only “Let ... and let”, not the continuous-image theorem clause used in step 1.2. - **Why fatal:** the visible fact widened the subdisc estimate, and the durable citation record did not cite a proposition at all. - **Repair:** [L5] now states the full disc and holomorphy assumptions; the contract quotes the full subdisc estimate and both clauses of the continuous-image theorem used for compact edge traces. - **Severity:** fatal. Alpha-c adjudicated confirmed_fatal and verified the repaired current disk text and owning batch contract.","adjudication_ref":["R7-3: Alpha-c confirmed_fatal"],"evidence":[{"path":"research/frontier-16-reader-7.md","anchor":"R7-3"}],"source":"alpha-c-6b"}
