research/frontier-12-dispatch/beta-batch-1-author.result.json:16:  "tail": "\n| Page | Items |\n|---|---:|\n| [The Field of Fractions and Localisation](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/abstract-algebra/the-field-of-fractions-and-localisation.md) | 22 |\n| [Localisation Examples](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/abstract-algebra/the-field-of-fractions-and-localisation-examples.md) | 8 |\n| [Splitting Fields](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/abstract-algebra/splitting-fields.md) | 18 |\n| [Splitting Fields Examples](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/abstract-algebra/splitting-fields-examples.md) | 8 |\n\nGate results:\n\n- Precheck: 49/49 proof-bearing items clean\n- Rendercheck: 60/60 files clean\n- Prosecheck: 4 pages, 0 errors and 0 warnings\n- Citecheck: 56/56 items clean\n- Strict proof contracts: 49/49, 0 errors and 0 warnings\n- Coverage: 97 harvested results, 0 errors and 0 warnings\n- Content policy: 56 items, 0 errors and 0 warnings\n- Plan validation: `OK`\n- No cross-page B-leaf violations\n\nMaterial departures from the scaffolded proof designs were:\n\n- Corrected the localization injectivity criterion to account for the house convention that zero is not itself called a zero divisor.\n- Restricted iterated localization to the reviewed \\(S,T\\subseteq R\\) formulation.\n- Made the first root field exactly \\(F(\\alpha)\\).\n- Rebuilt the factorial coordinate bound by its own strong induction.\n- Constructed an ambient splitting field before choosing arbitrary conjugates in the normality proof.\n- Proved the concrete maps into \\(\\mathbb Q\\) and \\(F(x)\\) injective rather than merely calling them embeddings.\n- Derived divisor-of-a-split-polynomial consequences inside the proofs from the exact UFD theorem.\n- Used group powers for \\(x^n-a\\), avoiding the real-only integer-power definition.\n- Added the finiteness argument required for endomorphisms to permute roots.\n- Transported the cubic monomial bound to the concrete splitting-field copy via uniqueness.\n- Grounded the repeated-root example in the exact square-divisibility definition and UFD uniqueness.\n- Constructed the nontrivial quadratic automorphism using Eisenstein and simple-root adjunction.\n- Corrected the normal-extension wording for nonmonic irreducibles by using their monic associates.\n- Added the exact Stacks prime-correspondence source, tag `00E3`.\n\nThe complete durable report is in [frontier-12-batch-1.notes.md](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/frontier-12-batch-1.notes.md), with synchronized [proof contracts](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/frontier-12-batch-1.proof-contracts.json) and [coverage record](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/frontier-12-batch-1.coverage.json).\n\nAll required claims closed honestly. No blocker, publication, audit metadata, or commit was introduced."
