research/frontier-12-audit-coverage.json:1993:      "reason": "Authored deps exceed the step-0 plan by four items, in two stages. (a) thm-fubini-over-a-region-between-continuous-graphs was added at step 5, when the author needed a named Jordan-measurability/integrability result to feed the symmetric assertion of thm-jordan-fubini-by-sections; the plan named only the Jordan-Fubini theorem. (b) At step 8b DeepSeek correctly objected that this theorem covers only vertical-graph regions, so it cannot license a Type II region (adjudicated confirmed_fatal, defect_type dependency_citation). The repair adds three published items so the transpose is written rather than assumed: def-type-i-type-ii-and-elementary-green-regions (the region class the Statement names, and its compactness), thm-linear-images-scale-jordan-content-by-absolute-determinant (the coordinate swap sigma(x,y)=(y,x) carries the bounded Jordan set sigma(D) back to D), and thm-continuous-functions-on-compact-jordan-sets-are-integrable (integrability of d_xQ over D and over each horizontal section). All four are published, all precede this page in reading order, and depcheck/fwdcheck confirm no cycle and no forward reference. See research/frontier-12-alpha-step8b.md and research/frontier-12-impact-audit.json."
