research/frontier-12-dispatch/beta-batch-5-author.result.json:16:  "tail": "Authored the complete authoritative Batch 5 scope: **82 items across four draft pages**. The dispatch’s 79-item count was stale; Alpha’s additions make the plan scope 37 + 11 + 28 + 6.\n\n- [Finite probability spaces and random variables](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/combinatorics/finite-probability-spaces-and-random-variables.md): 37\n- [Foundations examples](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/combinatorics/finite-probability-spaces-and-random-variables-examples.md): 11\n- [Finite probability and the probabilistic method](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/combinatorics/finite-probability-and-the-probabilistic-method.md): 28\n- [Method examples](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/combinatorics/finite-probability-and-the-probabilistic-method-examples.md): 6\n\nAll items are `status: draft`, `origin: session`, with component provenance. No B-leaf or AI-generated-statement dependency exists.\n\nDepartures from the scaffolded strategy:\n\n1. Narrowed the Erdős sum-free theorem to nonempty finite sets; the strict bound is false for the empty set.\n2. Expanded the Local Lemma conditional induction with explicit quotient events and positive denominators.\n3. Replaced the high-girth theorem’s asymptotic shortcut with finite inequalities and a separate `ell <= 2` case.\n4. Handled tournament-property cases `k=1,2` explicitly, including `(3/4)^8 < 1/9`.\n5. Realized the Bayes urn example on an explicit eight-outcome product space.\n6. Corrected the prime-congruence proof to use finite products and prime factorisation.\n7. Removed the scaffolded B-to-B dependency by making the false-linearity witness self-contained.\n\nFinal gates:\n\n- Precheck: 65/65 clean\n- Rendercheck: 86/86 clean\n- Prosecheck: 0 errors, 0 warnings\n- Citecheck: 82/82 clean\n- Strict proof contracts: 65/65 clean\n- Content policy: 82/82 clean\n- Coverage: 200 results, clean\n- Plan validation: acyclic, no forward/B-page/unresolved dependencies\n\nThe detailed durable report is in [batch notes](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/frontier-12-batch-5.notes.md), with synchronized [proof contracts](/Users/ianx/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/frontier-12-batch-5.proof-contracts.json). Nothing remains unclosed after the sum-free narrowing; no blockers and nothing published."
